." mdview manual page for macOS
.TH MDVIEW 1 "2025-12-09" "mdview 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdview \- render Markdown in the terminal with an internal viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdview
.RI [ \-h ]
.RI [ \-\-reflow ]
.RI [ \-\-reflow\-mode
.I MODE
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-noreflow ]
.RI [ \-V ]
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
mdview renders Markdown and plain text with ANSI styling and displays content
through its internal viewing engine. External pagers such as
.BR less (1)
and
.BR more (1)
are not used for display.
For pure text files, default behavior preserves source line breaks and
does not reflow unless reflow is explicitly enabled.
Markdown reflows to viewport width by default. Markdown tables may exceed
viewport width when minimum table sizing requires overflow.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B path
Path to a Markdown or text file to view.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-reflow
Enable reflow processing. If no explicit mode is supplied, prose mode is used.
.TP
.BR \-\-reflow\-mode " " MODE
Select reflow policy mode:
.IR prose ,
.IR all ,
or
.IR none .
.TP
.BR \-\-noreflow
Disable reflow in all cases (equivalent to mode none).
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Show the mdview version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B posix/mdview-help.txt
The shared POSIX help text derived from the argparse configuration. Keep this
file in sync with the parser when packaging the macOS man page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curses (3x),
.BR terminfo (5)
